# Metadata Standards

Every article should contain.

Clear title.

Clear description.

Logical URL.

Meaningful headings.

Semantic structure.

Accurate summaries.

Metadata should describe.

Not persuade.

---

# URL Standards

URLs should remain.

Simple.

Readable.

Timeless.

Stable.

Example.

```
brains.io/blog/startup-validation
```

Avoid dates.

Avoid unnecessary categories.

Avoid changing URLs.

---

# Heading Standards

One H1.

Logical H2 sections.

Supporting H3 headings.

Headings should answer questions.

Not tease information.

---

# Featured Snippets

Explain important concepts immediately.

Use concise definitions.

Follow with detailed explanations.

Help humans first.

Featured snippets become a natural outcome.

---

# Images

Every image should teach.

Avoid decorative graphics.

Prefer.

Diagrams.

Frameworks.

Decision trees.

Matrices.

Knowledge maps.

Visual explanations.

Images should become reference material.

---

# Schema Thinking

Structure content clearly.

Articles.

Guides.

Frameworks.

Definitions.

Case studies.

Templates.

Search engines understand structure.

Readers benefit from clarity.

---

# Content Freshness

Evergreen does not mean static.

Review important articles regularly.

Improve frameworks.

Update examples.

Expand research.

Strengthen internal links.

Knowledge compounds through revision.

---

# Measuring Success

